/** TOP-3: Whale. Figma "Whales" position. Art is 13.001 × 11.2002 and the
 *  path's bounding box fills that box EXACTLY on all four sides — every edge of
 *  the whale is flush with the art bounds, so any viewBox that equals the art
 *  bounds shaves the outermost antialiased row off whichever edge the rasterizer
 *  rounds against. That is the whole history of this glyph: e64ef8f5 ("cut off
 *  on the face") was the left edge, e752a5c7 ("needs to be closed") the top, and
 *  5f541284 came back a third time. Each fix padded one more edge and left the
 *  rest flush.
 *
 *  So: 0.1 of padding on ALL FOUR sides, not two. viewBox origin (-0.1, -0.1),
 *  size 13.201 × 11.4002 = art + 0.2 in each axis.
 *
 *  CALLERS MUST COMPENSATE. Figma's `icons/action` wrapper (5812:111846) insets
 *  the whale 6.25%/18.75%/12.49%/11.25% inside the 16px box, i.e. 13.0 × 11.2 of
 *  visible whale. Since the viewBox is now 0.2 taller than the art, a caller
 *  asking for `height: 11.4` gets 11.2 of actual whale — which is why the
 *  sidebar rows pass art 11.4 and not 11. Rendering at 11 (the old value, when
 *  the viewBox was only 0.1 over) draws the whale at 10.9 × 12.65, ~2.7% under
 *  the frame. */
